one proteins, CAST, RIM1, and Bassoon, in neurotransmitter release. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>164</volume>:<fpage>301</fpage>&#x02013;311.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14734538</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib29"><citation citation-type="journal">tom Dieck, S., L. Sanmarti-Vila, K. Langnaese, K. Richter, S. Kindler, A. Soyke, H. Wex, K.-H. Smalla, U. Kampf, J.T. Franzer, et al. <year>1998</year>. Bassoon, a novel zinc-finger CAG/glutamine-repeat protein selectively localized at the active zone of presynaptic nerve terminals. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>142</volume>:<fpage>499</fpage>&#x02013;509.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9679147</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><citation citation-type="journal">Turner, J., and M. Crossley. <year>2001</year>. The CtBP family: enigmatic and enzymatic transcriptional co-repressors. <source>Bioessays.</source> <volume>23</volume>:<fpage>683</fpage>&#x02013;690.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11494316</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib31"><citation citation-type="journal">Van Epps, H.A., M. Hayashi, L. Lucast, G.W. Stearns, J.B. Hurley, P. DeCamilli, and S.E. Brockerhoff. <year>2004</year>. The zebrafish nrc mutant reveals a role for the polyphosphoinositide phosphatase synaptojanin 1 in cone photoreceptor ribbon anchoring. <source>J. Neurosci.</source> <volume>24</volume>:<fpage>8641</fpage>&#x02013;8650.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15470129</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib32"><citation citation-type="journal">Vardinon-Friedman, H., T. Bresler, C.C. Garner, and N.E. Ziv. <year>2000</year>. Assembly of new individual excitatory synapses: time course and temporal order of synaptic molecule recruitment. <source>Neuron.</source> <volume>27</volume>:<fpage>57</fpage>&#x02013;69.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10939331</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib33"><citation citation-type="journal">von Gersdorff, H. <year>2001</year>. Synaptic ribbons: versatile signal transducers. <source>Neuron.</source> <volume>29<